messages:
maria: Heads up — found a mismatch between the API ref and the Node snippet for /v1/generate-stream. Docs show newline-delimited JSON but runtime streams SSE 'data: ...' lines. Node snippet does JSON.parse(chunk) and fails. Example:
```js
stream.on('data', chunk => {
  const obj = JSON.parse(chunk)
})
``` Need a quick docs patch + migration note.

kevin: Thanks — can you paste the failing error and confirm which route/model? I can try to repro locally.

maria: Error from customer: SyntaxError: Unexpected token d in JSON at position 0. Route: /v1/generate-stream. Snippet lives in docs/snippets/node/generate-stream.md.

sam: I can update the snippet to parse SSE lines. Proposed quick snippet:```js
stream.on('data', chunk => {
  const text = chunk.toString()
  const lines = text.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)
  lines.forEach(line => {
    if (!line.startsWith('data:')) return
    const payload = JSON.parse(line.replace(/^data:\s*/, ''))
    // handle payload.event / payload.data etc.
  })
})
``` Also add a one-liner: "If you use the SDK streaming helper, prefer sdk.stream(...) which yields parsed events."

olga: Agree. OpenAPI currently lists response content as application/json (array). That's wrong for SSE. We should change media-type to text/event-stream and update examples. I'll open a docs PR to update both the OpenAPI response and the Node/Python snippets.

docs-bot: PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/432 by olga — changes: openapi response media-type, node snippet, python snippet, short migration note. CI: docs-lint passed.

kevin: I'll add a small integration test in runtime that emits an SSE sample (data: {"event":"message","data":{...}}

) and verify docs example matches. Ping me with a test vector.

maria: Triage: customer is on Dedicated and hit this today. Short timeline: change the Node snippet + a migration note now, full schema/media-type change can be rolled tomorrow. Customer needs an immediate doc workaround.

sam: :thumbsup: I'll land the snippet change and the migration blurb referencing PR 432. Will add a note under "Streaming behavior" about SSE framing and the SDK helpers.

olga: Also update Python snippet — current example does `for chunk in stream: data = json.loads(chunk)` which will fail the same way. I'll patch both.

kevin: Runtime-side: I'll expose a tiny helper in the SDKs (sseParser) and document it in the Node snippet once landed. @maria can you confirm customer is okay using the helper?

maria: Confirmed. They can switch to parsed events or use non-streaming endpoint as fallback. Thanks.

sam: Landed change: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/432/files — docs preview build is up on staging. Patch included Node + Python snippets and short migration note.

olga: I'll follow up with a fuller migration guide at docs/migration/streaming-sse.md with examples and a small troubleshooting checklist. ETA: EOD.

maria: Thanks all — marking this resolved for the customer. Will reopen if anything else pops up.
